# Raspberry Pi 4 Self-Healing Yocto Distribution (RAUC A/B + HiveMQ AI Agent)

An industrial-grade Yocto embedded distribution targeting **Raspberry Pi 4 (64-bit)** with an autonomous C++ network self-healing agent, HiveMQ MQTT telemetry, and atomic Over-The-Air (OTA) updates using RAUC dual-bank A/B partitioning.

---

## Architecture Overview

```
                      +---------------------------------------+
                      |       Ubuntu ThinkPad (PC Agent)      |
                      |  - Anomaly Detection (AI Engine)      |
                      |  - Live Health & Telemetry Dashboard   |
                      |  - Built-in HTTP OTA Bundle Server    |
                      +-------------------+-------------------+
                                          |
                                    HiveMQ Broker
                              (broker.hivemq.com:1883)
                                          |
                      +-------------------+-------------------+
                      |      Raspberry Pi 4 (Embedded Node)   |
                      |                                       |
                      |  [Native C++ Local Agent]             |
                      |   - Auto Network Healer (wpa_cli,     |
                      |     DHCP renew, interface bounce)     |
                      |   - Hardware Telemetry (Temp, RAM)    |
                      |   - RAUC Slot Watchdog & 'mark-good'  |
                      |                                       |
                      |  [U-Boot + RAUC A/B Storage Engine]   |
                      |   - Slot A: /dev/mmcblk0p2 (Active)   |
                      |   - Slot B: /dev/mmcblk0p3 (Fallback) |
                      |   - Data:   /dev/mmcblk0p4 (Persist)  |
                      +---------------------------------------+
```

---

## Directory Structure

```
rpi-selfhealing-distro/
├── layers/
│   ├── poky/                     # Yocto Core & BitBake (Scarthgap)
│   ├── meta-raspberrypi/         # Raspberry Pi 4 BSP layer
│   ├── meta-openembedded/        # Core, Networking, and Python libraries
│   ├── meta-rauc/                # Robust Auto-Update Controller
│   └── meta-selfhealing/         # Custom Distro Layer
│       ├── conf/layer.conf
│       ├── recipes-core/
│       │   ├── images/selfhealing-image.bb
│       │   ├── bundles/selfhealing-bundle.bb
│       │   ├── local-agent/      # Native C++ self-healing daemon
│       │   │   ├── local-agent_1.0.bb
│       │   │   └── files/        # CMakeLists.txt, C++ sources, systemd unit
│       │   ├── rauc/             # system.conf & CA certificates
│       │   └── base-files/       # Persistent /data mount configuration
│       ├── recipes-bsp/
│       │   ├── rpi-u-boot-scr/   # RAUC boot script for U-Boot
│       │   └── u-boot/           # fw_env.config for userspace RAUC
│       ├── recipes-connectivity/
│       │   └── wpa-supplicant/   # Multi-SSID fallback Wi-Fi config
│       └── wic/
│           └── sdimage-dual-raspberrypi.wks
├── scripts/
│   ├── setup-workspace.sh        # Automates workspace setup on Ubuntu
│   └── generate-rauc-keys.sh     # Generates OpenSSL RSA keys for RAUC
└── pc-agent/
    ├── agent.py                  # AI Agent console on ThinkPad
    └── requirements.txt
```

---

## Quick Start on Your Ubuntu machie

### Step 1: Copy/Sync the Workspace
Copy this directory to your ThinkPad:
```bash
# E.g., via rsync or git
cp -r rpi-selfhealing-distro ~/
cd ~/rpi-selfhealing-distro
```

### Step 2: Initialize Workspace & Layers
```bash
chmod +x scripts/*.sh
./scripts/setup-workspace.sh
```

### Step 3: Build the SD Card Image & Initial RAUC Bundle
```bash
cd ~/rpi-selfhealing-distro/build
source ../layers/poky/oe-init-build-env .

# 1. Build initial dual-bank SD card image (~1.5 hours on modern CPU)
bitbake selfhealing-image

# 2. Build the OTA update bundle (.raucb)
bitbake selfhealing-bundle
```

The output files will be in:
`tmp/deploy/images/raspberrypi4-64/`
- `selfhealing-image-raspberrypi4-64.wic.bz2` -> Flash to SD card using `bmaptool` or BalenaEtcher.
- `selfhealing-bundle-raspberrypi4-64.raucb` -> Signed OTA update file.

---

## Flash & Initial Boot

1. Insert SD card into ThinkPad and flash:
   ```bash
   cd ~/rpi-selfhealing-distro/build/tmp/deploy/images/raspberrypi4-64/
   bmaptool copy selfhealing-image-raspberrypi4-64.rootfs.wic.bz2 /dev/sdX
   ```
2. Insert SD card into Raspberry Pi 4 and boot.
3. The board boots into **Slot A**, loads `local-agent`, connects to Wi-Fi, and reaches HiveMQ.

---

## Running the ThinkPad PC AI Agent

```bash
cd ~/rpi-selfhealing-distro/pc-agent
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python3 agent.py
```

### Performing an Over-The-Air (OTA) Update
1. Make changes to any recipe in `meta-selfhealing` (e.g. update C++ agent or install new tool).
2. Re-generate bundle:
   ```bash
   bitbake selfhealing-bundle
   ```
3. In `agent.py` console on ThinkPad:
   ```text
   ai-agent> host ../build/tmp/deploy/images/raspberrypi4-64/
   ai-agent> ota http://<THINKPAD_IP>:8080/selfhealing-bundle-raspberrypi4-64.raucb
   ```
4. The Raspberry Pi 4 downloads the bundle, writes it to **Slot B**, reboots atomically into Slot B, and verifies system health before marking Slot B good. If Slot B fails to boot, U-Boot automatically falls back to Slot A!
